# PLAN-920 legacy-AVM immutable-assignment diagnostic suite — the typed-fact
# closure of the M1 B18 avm cell (gap-audit F-INFRA-3 / `gap:legacy-b18-infra`).
# The old codegen now emits the REAL typed NameError::ImmutableAssignment
# (miette `auto_name_E0203`) from all three immutable-reject branches, so the
# avm adapter's staged classification (classify_staged) judges the rejection
# as a Language/type fact — the 2026-11-01 908T04 re-probe's infra-only
# observation is closed by production facts, never by text matching:
#
#   negative  src/B18.at                  — the frozen original (bare `x = 2`
#                                           expr-statement on a `let`)
#   negative  immutable-avm-920/B18C.at   — same family via compound `x += 2`
#   negative  immutable-avm-920/TOP.at    — same family at script top level
#                                           (statement wrapper path)
#   neighbor  src/NB18.at                 — `let`→`var`, real run, result 2
#   neighbor  immutable-avm-920/NB18S.at  — same-name inner `var` over outer
#                                           `let`: legal writes, never
#                                           over-rejected (slot-reuse result
#                                           6 is the legacy display fact)
#
# Strict-boundary counter-controls (forged B18-text Msg, other-family typed
# codes, run-trap channel separation, IO/panic infra) are parent-side unit
# controls (auto-lang-core vm::immutable_assign_920) — a mutating fixture
# cannot be a committed green case (PLAN-911 precedent).
# The stmt_emit Store-guard branch is production-unreachable (only
# StoreKind::Field passes `!is_new_declaration` and Field statements compile
# via the TypeDecl path) — locked AST-level in the same unit file; no source
# case is fabricated for it.

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ace.m1.ia920.b18"
  tags: ["ace-m1", "diagnostic", "immutable-avm-920"]
  links: ["PLAN-920"]
  source: { file: "src/B18.at", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "autovm", adapter: "avm", action: "run",
      expect: { completion: { stage: "type", code: "auto_name_E0203" } } },
  ]
}
```

